            <ArticleTitle>[The prediction of the probability of the development of a myocardial infarct in patients with unstable angina].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>26-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary reserve and functional state of myocardium were studied in 27 patients with unstable angina and myocardial infarction which had developed in spite of the treatment. Non-invasive study included stress-tests (transesophageal electrocardiostimulation, bicycle ergometry [correction of veloergometry)], echocardiography and Holter's monitoring. Possibility of early forming of risk group with consequent optimization of the treatment was shown.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
